#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133881 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133697 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d42243ea-58fc-53f6-a0b6-f995bf1d697c" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting the Curl of a Vector Field"}] :question/id #uuid "cb99a3e1-9cd1-5335-b20c-01ad598d14bf" :question/math-academy-id "e-8929" :question/problem "![](images/71/71c58bf1b0fe4259ac50633a457f6a76639c0a0c188b66cce5e0fc3c7e5b0329.png)\n\n \n\nConsider the vector field $\\mathbf F(x,y,z),$ shown above. Given that $\\mathbf F(x,y,z)$ is independent of $z,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $\\textrm{curl}\\,\\mathbf F = \\mathbf 0$\n\n- $\\textrm{curl}\\, \\mathbf F \\neq \\mathbf 0$\n\n- $\\mathbf F$ is irrotational\n\n- $\\textrm{curl}\\, \\mathbf F$ points in the positive $z$-direction." :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\textrm{curl}\\,\\mathbf F$ denotes the curl of the vector field $\\mathbf F.$\n\nTo understand intuitively whether a vector field has curl at a point $P$, imagine that our vector field $\\mathbf F$ represents the velocity field of a stream of flowing water. We place a paddlewheel at $P$ with the axis of rotation pointing in the $z$-direction, and we note whether the paddlewheel rotates or not.\n\n- If the paddlewheel is forced to rotate due to the action of the water, then the vector field has curl, i.e., $\\textrm{curl}\\,\\mathbf F \\neq  \\mathbf 0.$\n\n- If the paddlewheel does not rotate due to the action of the water, then the velocity field has zero curl, i.e., $\\textrm{curl}\\,\\mathbf F =  \\mathbf 0.$\n\n![](images/86/86aee33cdfa96ac0a61468cc9657e791e399f31c024cdbc3a932193dc897d534.png)\n\nIf $\\textrm{curl}\\,\\mathbf F = \\mathbf 0$ everywhere in $\\mathbb R^3$, we say that $\\mathbf F$ is irrotational.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is false, whereas statement II is true. If a paddlewheel were placed at any point $P$ in the manner described above, it would rotate counterclockwise. Therefore, $\\textrm{curl}\\,\\mathbf F \\neq \\mathbf 0.$\n\n- Statements III is false. Since $\\textrm{curl}\\,\\mathbf F \\neq \\mathbf 0,$ the vector field $\\mathbf F$ is not irrotational.\n\n- Statement IV is true. Using our right hand, if we wrap our fingers in the direction of rotation (counterclockwise), our thumb will point upward. Therefore, $\\textrm{curl}\\,\\mathbf F$ points upward, in the direction of increasing $z.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and IV only.\""} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d42243ea-58fc-53f6-a0b6-f995bf1d697c" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048917}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134062 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d42243ea-58fc-53f6-a0b6-f995bf1d697c" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting the Curl of a Vector Field"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "64adfa84-016b-5b75-bfaa-1a8a86ec6cff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437398} {:answer/id #uuid "74db0023-87ca-59a4-a5bd-f3ec8e8116b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437399}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "74db0023-87ca-59a4-a5bd-f3ec8e8116b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437399} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8d82e25-5382-533b-84b7-01e9f7a1d6d9" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438728} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8567ee77-d4f1-5260-9f23-476c33065db6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437400} {:answer/id #uuid "a70669e9-818c-5056-9e48-6b53420d42e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437401}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8567ee77-d4f1-5260-9f23-476c33065db6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437400} :answer-field/id #uuid "a4ff09e7-c874-5a69-a376-7cc151c1b301" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438729} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bdbd1a0c-db83-58a6-82a4-5124aff61305" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437402} {:answer/id #uuid "66a86276-9dec-5106-ae18-146b9a8a0341" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437403}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "66a86276-9dec-5106-ae18-146b9a8a0341" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437403} :answer-field/id #uuid "76eb44c2-5da3-5456-a3ae-c27f914fb121" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438730} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c36d028-9a19-523f-8a50-c043c1583d10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437404} {:answer/id #uuid "f9c4fd28-7364-51cd-9702-c77f2ad2fba7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437405}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6c36d028-9a19-523f-8a50-c043c1583d10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437404} :answer-field/id #uuid "455d8cf9-d20d-599d-bbf0-180199060744" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438731}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7a72f589-a1bb-57d0-9bf2-23704868e98f" :question/math-academy-id "q-105092" :question/problem "![](images/38/38a7ae83a66a2c1ff6a012b9405c6621b0c0a162018065549e75a1d08bc04d44.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y,z),$ shown above. Given that $F(x,y,z)$ is independent of $z,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$\n- **II.** $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0$\n- **III.** $F$ is irrotational\n- **IV.** $\\text{curl}\\,F$ points in the negative $z$-direction." :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{curl}\\,F$ denotes the curl of the vector field $F.$\n\nTo understand intuitively whether a vector field has curl at a point $P$, imagine that our vector field $F$ represents the velocity field of a stream of flowing water. We place a paddlewheel at $P$ with the axis of rotation pointing in the $z$-direction, and we note whether the paddlewheel rotates or not.\n\n- If the paddlewheel does not rotate due to the action of the water, then the velocity field has zero curl, i.e., $\\text{curl}\\,F=0.$\n\n- If the paddlewheel is forced to rotate due to the action of the water, then the vector field has curl, i.e., $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0.$\n\n![](images/59/594106633e422d24b9fea113d24fb6367fdef5ac52724931860e4163e33ce992.png)\n\nMoreover, if $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$ everywhere in ${R}^{3}$, we say that $F$ is irrotational.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true, whereas statement II is false. If a paddlewheel were placed at any point $P$ in the manner described above, it would not rotate. Therefore, $\\text{curl}\\,F=0.$\n\n- Statements III is true. Since $\\text{curl}\\,F=0,$ the vector field $F$ is irrotational.\n\n- Statement IV is false. Since $\\text{curl}\\,F=0,$ it points in neither the positive nor the negative $z$-direction.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134063 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d42243ea-58fc-53f6-a0b6-f995bf1d697c" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting the Curl of a Vector Field"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ba17fd4c-8a29-5e53-98c2-ac71e936d451" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :