swer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437468} :answer-field/id #uuid "daa53b8b-f892-5eaf-a4df-840413a09c4a" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438763}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d7d9f8f8-5aac-59da-a7d3-267484c84687" :question/math-academy-id "q-105667" :question/problem "![](images/77/773ff9d880deed92f8034d6949cfee85edbcdf735c8e125f1ec5762137fadb9c.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y,z),$ shown above. Given that $F(x,y,z)$ is independent of $z,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$\n- **II.** $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0$\n- **III.** $F$ is irrotational\n- **IV.** $\\text{curl}\\,F$ points in the negative $z$-direction." :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{curl}\\,F$ denotes the curl of the vector field $F.$\n\nTo understand intuitively whether a vector field has curl at a point $P$, imagine that our vector field $F$ represents the velocity field of a stream of flowing water. We place a paddlewheel at $P$ with the axis of rotation pointing in the $z$-direction, and we note whether the paddlewheel rotates or not.\n\n- If the paddlewheel does not rotate due to the action of the water, then the velocity field has zero curl, i.e., $\\text{curl}\\,F=0.$\n\n- If the paddlewheel is forced to rotate due to the action of the water, then the vector field has curl, i.e., $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0.$\n\n![](images/4e/4e344a0a1f6b0c535c5ba08ee8c87914cf5e7009600f45732023720048b4c493.png)\n\nMoreover, if $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$ everywhere in ${R}^{3}$, we say that $F$ is irrotational.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true, whereas statement II is false. If a paddlewheel were placed at any point $P$ in the manner described above, it would not rotate. Therefore, $\\text{curl}\\,F=0.$\n\n- Statements III is true. Since $\\text{curl}\\,F=0,$ the vector field $F$ is irrotational.\n\n- Statements IV is false. Since $\\text{curl}\\,F=0,$ it points in neither the positive nor the negative $z$-direction.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241108 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d42243ea-58fc-53f6-a0b6-f995bf1d697c" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting the Curl of a Vector Field"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "87f8866c-3269-5305-94e0-80d60142b798" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437470} {:answer/id #uuid "ceaad2e3-2efd-5e19-bb7f-b57ea3fc6e7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437471}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "87f8866c-3269-5305-94e0-80d60142b798" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437470} :answer-field/id #uuid "0c08d5d7-5b76-5798-9849-c11e4265495c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438764} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "af0ccef4-0d9f-5258-a00a-2d3b70919956" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437472} {:answer/id #uuid "e6f2d444-ce1a-575d-8dd5-cb8eca23b4aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437473}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e6f2d444-ce1a-575d-8dd5-cb8eca23b4aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437473} :answer-field/id #uuid "05bb4ba6-a345-5135-97e0-a2bde6d14a93" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438765} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f909166-7a9f-5343-b5ec-b4d1d3560f78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437474} {:answer/id #uuid "7e3f9244-257c-5be9-95ea-d30230d49bf6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437475}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e3f9244-257c-5be9-95ea-d30230d49bf6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437475} :answer-field/id #uuid "690da8d3-c31e-5a96-8f2e-4923d49f0a94" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438766} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a1438c53-192f-52c6-a875-55bb696d0ded" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437476} {:answer/id #uuid "bb2db5d5-ff4e-5705-a9a3-8abc334919c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437477}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a1438c53-192f-52c6-a875-55bb696d0ded" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437476} :answer-field/id #uuid "91d192c0-fb0c-5d05-a1b4-1e76869a1358" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438767}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2c2154fc-c947-5ba9-b169-f98f4fea25a5" :question/math-academy-id "q-105669" :question/problem "![](images/24/2414de6e2129d4fceaae304d16f9be0c91a545e5a8544b2033f353ddb2e581b9.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y,z),$ shown above. Given that $F(x,y,z)$ is independent of $z,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$\n- **II.** $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0$\n- **III.** $\\text{curl}\\,F$ points in the positive $z$-direction.\n- **IV.** $F$ is irrotational" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{curl}\\,F$ denotes the curl of the vector field $F.$\n\nTo understand intuitively whether a vector field has curl at a point $P$, imagine that our vector field $F$ represents the velocity field of a stream of flowing water. We place a paddlewheel at $P$ with the axis of rotation pointing in the $z$-direction, and we note whether the paddlewheel rotates or not.\n\n- If the paddlewheel is forced to rotate due to the action of the water, then the vector field has curl, i.e., $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0.$\n\n- If the paddlewheel does not rotate due to the action of the water, then the velocity field has zero curl, i.e., $\\text{curl}\\,F=0.$\n\n![](images/86/86aee33cdfa96ac0a61468cc9657e791e399f31c024cdbc3a932193dc897d534.png)\n\nIf $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$ everywhere in ${R}^{3}$, we say that $F$ is irrotational.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement II is true, whereas statement I is false. If a paddlewheel were placed at any point $P$ in the manner described above, it would rotate counterclockwise. Therefore, $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Using our right hand, if we wrap our fingers in the direction of rotation (counterclockwise), our thumb will point away from the screen. Therefore, $\\text{curl}\\,F$ also points away from the screen, in the direction of increasing $z.$\n\n- Statement IV is false. Since $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0,$ the vector field $F$ is not irrotational.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241110 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d42243ea-58fc-53f6-a0b6-f995bf1d697c" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting the Curl of a Vector Field"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ecf86ba1-b225-5f4e-a85f-182bd2bdbc53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437478} {:answer/id #uuid "c7744411-0aa5-54ef-9c74-d6ca7e53bdb6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437479}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid