ices [{:answer/id #uuid "46189e0a-937f-5303-a19e-e8e9671daedc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437870} {:answer/id #uuid "a33bbeb3-b68d-5ea0-b9c4-a6bc64ed2f6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437871}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "46189e0a-937f-5303-a19e-e8e9671daedc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437870} :answer-field/id #uuid "36112e37-bcb8-5a8d-a232-63977d54a9c7" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438964}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f317d036-e0ac-5288-a673-4543ead19ce4" :question/math-academy-id "q-131366" :question/problem "![](images/78/781a4e33b8b55762b2dcb7575d08315b5842f83d6d78a5136a1c353eefd3069d.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y,z),$ shown above. Given that $F(x,y,z)$ is independent of $z,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$\n- **II.** $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0$\n- **III.** $F$ is irrotational\n- **IV.** $\\text{curl}\\,F$ points in the negative $z$-direction." :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{curl}\\,F$ denotes the curl of the vector field $F.$\n\nTo understand intuitively whether a vector field has curl at a point $P$, imagine that our vector field $F$ represents the velocity field of a stream of flowing water. We place a paddlewheel at $P$ with the axis of rotation pointing in the $z$-direction, and we note whether the paddlewheel rotates or not.\n\n- If the paddlewheel does not rotate due to the action of the water, then the velocity field has zero curl, i.e., $\\text{curl}\\,F=0.$\n\n- If the paddlewheel is forced to rotate due to the action of the water, then the vector field has curl, i.e., $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0.$\n\n![](images/97/979b63f21e56924bd7880f9487cf829089e38cf14d287e70196c7a661e41f97f.png)\n\nMoreover, if $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$ everywhere in ${R}^{3}$, we say that $F$ is irrotational.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true, whereas statement II is false. If a paddlewheel were placed at any point $P$ in the manner described above, it would not rotate. Therefore, $\\text{curl}\\,F=0.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $\\text{curl}\\,F=0,$ the vector field $F$ is irrotational.\n\n- Statement IV is false. Since $\\text{curl}\\,F=0,$ it points in neither the positive nor the negative $z$-direction.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382833 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d42243ea-58fc-53f6-a0b6-f995bf1d697c" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting the Curl of a Vector Field"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d228b638-d4d7-5016-bf8d-0f56d5c4fadc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437454} {:answer/id #uuid "95914e2c-927b-55a2-922e-4d9800a2f38d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437455}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d228b638-d4d7-5016-bf8d-0f56d5c4fadc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437454} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b934add-e755-50b4-b067-100e72fc3b58" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438756} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0bd1d98c-7ae9-55ca-9482-d88b90b0af24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437456} {:answer/id #uuid "e43b1943-3654-567b-9fed-68e4254f3b7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437457}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e43b1943-3654-567b-9fed-68e4254f3b7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437457} :answer-field/id #uuid "c6ddf4cd-c05f-5097-8310-bbb48f377de3" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438757} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e686502-6511-5a87-9141-3f040b14bb72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437458} {:answer/id #uuid "d0bb29aa-53cb-587d-8e87-04375c2d7a7a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437459}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d0bb29aa-53cb-587d-8e87-04375c2d7a7a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437459} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8779a01-b29f-51f0-ab0b-183634a90544" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438758} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f0077624-dbc3-55a6-9c6d-142323470d70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437460} {:answer/id #uuid "3165d50d-3b7d-5943-9785-4266dd0bd54a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437461}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f0077624-dbc3-55a6-9c6d-142323470d70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437460} :answer-field/id #uuid "1bdf6bee-a19c-5f09-acb1-0c8cf50d5033" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438759}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b44da0aa-9add-572b-86e2-310e134b6864" :question/math-academy-id "q-105664" :question/problem "![](images/56/5643e87bfb5dfb5c29750f48abffe2443bf656901d74a47a0aa39bddfd0c1590.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y,z),$ shown above. Given that $F(x,y,z)$ is independent of $z,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$\n- **II.** $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0$\n- **III.** $\\text{curl}\\,F$ points in the positive $z$-direction.\n- **IV.** $F$ is irrotational" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{curl}\\,F$ denotes the curl of the vector field $F.$\n\nTo understand intuitively whether a vector field has a curl at a point $P$, imagine that our vector field $F$ represents the velocity field of a stream of flowing water. We place a paddlewheel at $P$ with the axis of rotation pointing in the $z$-direction, and we note whether the paddlewheel rotates or not.\n\n- If the paddlewheel is forced to rotate due to the action of the water, then the vector field has curl, i.e., $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0.$\n\n- If the paddlewheel does not rotate due to the action of the water, then the velocity field has zero curl, i.e., $\\text{curl}\\,F=0.$\n\n![](images/86/86aee33cdfa96ac0a61468cc9657e791e399f31c024cdbc3a932193dc897d534.png)\n\nIf $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$ everywhere in ${R}^{3}$, we say that $F$ is irrotational.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement II is true, whereas statement I is false. If a paddlewheel were placed at any point $P$ in the manner described above, it would rotate clockwise. Therefore, $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Using our right hand, if we wrap our fingers in the direction of rotation (counterclockwise), our thumb will point away from the screen. Therefore, $\\text{curl}\\,F$ also points away from the screen, in the direction of increasing $z.$\n\n- Statement IV is false. Since $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0,$ the vector field $F$ is not irrotational.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382840 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d42243ea-58fc-53f6-a0b6-f995bf1d697c" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting the Curl of a Vector Field"}] :questi