b/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438778} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e6a54cb-d3b8-527e-8166-9d17d4c66cfb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437500} {:answer/id #uuid "f7668637-64a8-52ae-aa22-7ac35611bf2e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437501}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e6a54cb-d3b8-527e-8166-9d17d4c66cfb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437500} :answer-field/id #uuid "b01a01c4-08c1-5b79-8565-85e0e916e53a" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438779}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "73b73866-28ec-57e7-b02e-d1bd053c3918" :question/math-academy-id "q-105693" :question/problem "![](images/10/10a9960200e87e1b7b8a38789d5f70f29e48ad1f0a6e2913713da90c532eca6e.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y,z),$ shown above. Given that $F(x,y,z)$ is independent of $z,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$\n- **II.** $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0$\n- **III.** $F$ is not irrotational\n- **IV.** $\\text{curl}\\,F$ points in the negative $z$-direction." :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{curl}\\,F$ denotes the curl of the vector field $F.$\n\nTo understand intuitively whether a vector field has curl at a point $P$, imagine that our vector field $F$ represents the velocity field of a stream of flowing water. We place a paddlewheel at $P$ with the axis of rotation pointing in the $z$-direction, and we note whether the paddlewheel rotates or not.\n\n- If the paddlewheel does not rotate due to the action of the water, then the velocity field has zero curl, i.e., $\\text{curl}\\,F=0.$\n\n- If the paddlewheel is forced to rotate due to the action of the water, then the vector field has curl, i.e., $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0.$\n\n![](images/59/594106633e422d24b9fea113d24fb6367fdef5ac52724931860e4163e33ce992.png)\n\nMoreover, if $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$ everywhere in ${R}^{3}$, we say that $F$ is irrotational.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true, whereas statement II is false. If a paddlewheel were placed at any point $P$ in the manner described above, it would not rotate. Therefore, $\\text{curl}\\,F=0.$\n\n- Statements III and IV are false. Since $\\text{curl}\\,F=0,$ the vector field $F$ is irrotational. And, since $\\text{curl}\\,F=0,$ it points in neither the positive nor the negative $z$-direction.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409610 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d42243ea-58fc-53f6-a0b6-f995bf1d697c" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting the Curl of a Vector Field"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8286c6dd-7fea-5018-b722-69a0848b0bcc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437502} {:answer/id #uuid "5d52abdf-7ac5-55e3-92ae-9aec71a85bbf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437503}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8286c6dd-7fea-5018-b722-69a0848b0bcc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437502} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb53bf33-5552-5395-8fd4-4d42b50a2a01" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438780} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a4939bd9-e529-5af3-b533-59e09598d0e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437504} {:answer/id #uuid "2b9d89e5-98a9-5520-8de9-5ddb178c0664" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437505}] :answer-field/corre